  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Typescript poem reproduced on torn white paper mounted on a decorated brown-paper banner, which is glued at the top edge onto the inside of a paper cover. The cover is wrapped in crushed, hand-painted paper (light blue and tan) onto which are mounted printed and hand-colored paper cutouts. A cutout "tower window" in the front cover reveals the banner's illustration of a bell with a moveable clapper, a white-paper cutout of a line drawing of a blindfolded woman hanging upside down; the "clapper" is inserted through the back of the banner.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">The banner unfolded measures 47 cm.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Part of a collection of handmade books, most with cords for hanging (literatura de cordel), published by Ediciones Vigía under the auspices of the Cuban Ministry of Culture.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
